#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Update the development paper from sealed controller and protected-scope evidence."""
import csv,shutil,time
from pathlib import Path
from retained_prefix_workflow import D,read,write,sha

r=read(D/'native_scope_policy_summary_02.json');p=read(D/'protected_native_scope_summary_01.json');assert r['passed'] and p['passed']
paper=D/'paper';data=paper/'data'
with (data/'native_scope_policy_v14.csv').open('w') as f:
 w=csv.writer(f);w.writerow(['batch','policy','scope','accepted_steps','CPD_ns','SB_pairs','CB_sources','wirelength','setup_better_vs_initial','setup_worse_vs_initial','fixed_initial_near_0.2ns','current_near_0.2ns','shared_controller_seconds'])
 for b in r['batches']:
  for policy,o in b['policies'].items():
   v=o['final'];m=v['resources'];c=o['comparison_to_initial'];w.writerow([Path(b['batch']).name,policy,b['scope'],o['accepted_steps'],format(v['cpd_ns'],'.17g'),m['sb_pairs_used'],m['cb_crossing_output_sources_used'],m['planar_wirelength_excluding_sb_half_nodes'],c['setup_improved'],c['setup_regressed'],v['near_fixed_initial_components'],v['near_current_components'],b['costs']['complete_orchestrator_seconds']])
text=r'''\paragraph{Autonomous native repair from an unmodified strong starting route.}
The unified controller selects connections from each accepted state's native STA, queries capacity-feasible extensions, constructs a joint conflict scope when necessary, and lets the native serial router choose every replacement path. Occupancy is updated after each attachment. Complete candidates receive independent physical checks and native FULL/STA; rejected states leave the immutable accepted route unchanged. An exact state/request cache shares repeated attempts across the two policy branches. The initial R1 route is the sealed, unmodified strong route, not an injected intermediate repair.

Single attempts on 6587/pin~4 and 6590/pin~4 preserve the complete timing plateau and are rejected. Joint repair of these targets, with four automatically identified blocking branches, reaches 5.854659868020917 ns from 6.018101128546505 ns, improving 246 setup components without regressions. Both policies accept. Fresh STA selects 76/pin~1 and 48/pin~1; their joint successor reaches 5.832274663220005 ns. Strict CPD accepts this second step, whereas endpoint-Pareto rejects its 0.371651154 ns loss at \texttt{Mp[12].D[0]} and retains its own first-step state. The strict branch's next six-connection frontier produces a legal 6.285112431 ns candidate, which is rejected. Thus this fully automatic native trajectory obtains the earlier best local CPD, 3.087792\% below the unmodified strong R1, without an injected first repair. It uses 40 SB pairs, 970 CB sources and planar wirelength 218245, compared with the original 39, 969 and 218164. This is one-circuit development evidence, not general promotion.

Relative to the original R1 endpoint vector, strict CPD improves 254 setup components and regresses one; endpoint-Pareto improves 246 and regresses none. The fixed initial 0.2 ns endpoint window shrinks from three components to one and two respectively. Windows recentered on each final state's own worst slack contain eighteen and fourteen components; these moving counts must not be read as the same fixed cohort. The unchanged native default constraints contain \texttt{virtual\_io\_clock}, \texttt{clk} and \texttt{clk\_mem}; no new SDC is supplied. The fixed vector contains 14032 setup/domain components over 13744 endpoints. CPD and vector decisions use the native full-precision numbers with no acceptance epsilon, while increased negative hold violations remain forbidden.

\paragraph{Released scope contributes beyond selection and full-device search.}
A matched native control starts from the same unmodified R1 and receives the same current-STA selector, full-device search, native cost objective and single/joint acceptance opportunities, but releases only the target branches. Both policy branches remain at 6.018101128546505 ns. The successful first conflict-scope repair additionally releases 1429/pin~1, 1967/pin~1, 6563/pin~1 and 7963/pin~2. Therefore selection and extra full-device target repair alone do not explain this first gain. Scope differs intentionally in this ablation; the earlier native/external engine comparisons retain their matched scopes. Exact previously completed single attempts and joint query results are reused after source state, request, normalized native command, objective and input checks. A preliminary reuse-controller assertion incorrectly included batch registration provenance in input identity; it stopped before any native call. Its failure is retained, and an independent corrected controller excludes only registration metadata not consumed by the VPR command.

\paragraph{Complete prototype cost is dominated by state preparation and checking.}
The two-policy conflict-scope R1 controller takes 631.358 s, including rejected work and cache handling. Nonoverlapping child times are 249.654 s for query/candidate audits, 196.460 s for candidate FULL/STA wrappers, 73.792 s for capacity/relaxed-query preparation and joint search, 72.494 s for native repair wrappers, and 23.328 s for scope preparation; 15.631 s occurs outside children. The native transactions themselves total only 1.979 s and are nested within the native wrappers. Five distinct native transactions make 66 connection-search attempts; the endpoint branch reuses common-state work. The target-only control costs 102.544 s incrementally, with one new native transaction and five searches; its reused work prevents interpreting the ratio as independent policy speedup. Continuing the earlier accepted native state costs 177.302 s, including a rejected candidate, versus 1.406 s inside its transaction. These measurements begin from existing legal routes and exclude generating those original routes. They are additional prototype-flow costs, not formal cold-start complete-routing benchmarks, and use no historical U timing.

\paragraph{Protecting a previous victim moves the bottleneck; joint capacity constrains the remaining potential.}
At 5.832274663 ns, only 5490/pin~5 and 6591/pin~4 among the six worst connections have positive relaxed fixed-tree delay potential, approximately 7.639 ps each. The first joint scope releases 21 connections and worsens 1388 setup components. A current-STA rule identifies the released 6589/pin~4 prefix as having only about 7.639 ps headroom. Reserving this prefix still admits compatible improving target paths, but their new conflict scope affects 25 connections. Native recovery preserves the protected prefix and lowers both target delays, yet the critical loss migrates to 6592/pin~4. The candidate remains legal at 6.285112430504114 ns, worsens 1387 setup components and is rejected by both policies. This control takes 87.245 s, including 1.757 s inside native recovery and 47 connection-search attempts. Target potential and a legal transaction do not imply CPD improvement.

The next diagnostic protects all eight current non-target prefixes whose slack headroom is within the maximum target gain, including newly encountered competitors. Each target separately retains its 7.639 ps potential, but joint conflict splitting identifies capacity-one IPIN 82116 as necessary for either strict local improvement. Forbidding this IPIN on either target produces an exact distance of 0.856978293883870 ns, its original delay, so the two gains cannot coexist with these eight prefixes fixed. This is a conditional residual-graph result, not a global routing or endpoint optimum. Protection is stronger than a timing budget: equal-delay victim relocation, different retained-tree scope and upstream changes remain untested possibilities. The next registered branch permits current-STA-budgeted victim alternatives and compares a slack-offset objective with raw connection-delay selection, retaining whole-transaction FULL/STA acceptance.
'''
(data/'native_scope_policy_discussion_v14.tex').write_text(text)
main=paper/'main.tex';s=main.read_text();needle='\\input{data/native_scope_policy_discussion_v14.tex}'
assert needle not in s;s=s.replace('\\section{Conclusion}',needle+'\n\n\\section{Conclusion}');main.write_text(s)
with (paper/'claims_evidence.md').open('a') as f:
 f.write('\n| C93 | 未人工修复的强R1起点可由原生current-STA控制器自主取得两步严格CPD收益 | [自动轨迹与完整成本](../native_scope_policy_summary_02.json)、[状态与资源表](data/native_scope_policy_v14.csv) | 6.018101128546505→5.854659868020917→5.832274663220005ns；strict254setup改善1退化，endpoint只接受首步246改善0退化。strict40SB970CB218245wire；无手动目标注入，当前STA每次接受后更新；单电路开发、不推广 |\n')
 f.write('| C94 | 同当前STA和全设备原生搜索，只有目标分支的对照不能取得首步收益 | [范围对照](../current_sta_policy_native_target_only_02/completion.json)、[复用回执](../current_sta_policy_native_target_only_02/reuse_receipts.json) | 两策略均0接受/6.018101129ns；conflict成功首步额外释放4阻塞分支。此次有意改变scope以隔离范围贡献；不冒充相同scope引擎差异 |\n')
 f.write('| C95 | 完整修复控制器计时揭示状态检查而非原生查询核心占主导 | [逐进程成本](../current_sta_policy_native_R1_01/process_costs.json)、[复用身份检查失败记录](../current_sta_policy_native_target_only_01/failure.json) | R1共享两策略631.358s，其中native核心1.979s已包含于72.494s native包装器；5事务66搜索。target-only102.544s为共享复用后的新增成本，不作速度比。初次身份断言失败0native；旧U时间不用于新原型 |\n')
 f.write('| C96 | 保护旧受害者只迁移瓶颈，全当前STA前缀参考暴露容量1入口竞争 | [机制与条件界](../protected_native_scope_summary_01.json)、[下一时序预算实验](../native_timing_budget_scope_experiment_01.json) | 保护6589p4后，两目标确实缩短但6592p4变差，合法6.285112431ns双拒绝；25连接47搜索。全8近关键前缀保留时，两目标改善都必须占IPIN82116，禁用后的精确下界等于各自原延迟，不能共同缩短。局部保留树条件结论，非全局STA最优；允许等延迟victim换路/调整retainedscope继续研究 |\n')
with (paper/'mechanisms_and_ablation.md').open('a') as f:f.write('\nC93–C96：原生current-STA从未修复R1自动取得两步CPD收益；同选择器/full-device机会的target-only对照无首步收益，释放范围贡献得到隔离。保护旧受害者真实生效仍迁移瓶颈；全当前STA保护给出IPIN容量条件证据，下一比较有时序预算的替代victim路径/retained范围，不能把7.639ps查询潜力当最终QoR。完整流程成本与原生核心分开，复用和身份断言失败保留。[汇总](../native_scope_policy_summary_02.json)、[条件容量](../protected_native_scope_summary_01.json)。\n')
with (paper/'README.md').open('a') as f:f.write('\nC93–C96新增自动原生修复、目标范围对照及近关键受影响前缀容量证据。严格分支从封存强R1自主到5.832274663ns；代码、论文和证据均为f7167bd之后本地新增，未推送。Tf自动原生批次另行登记运行，不把本轮局部operator终态当科研终止。\n')
ledger=data/'evidence_v14_ledger.json';history=data/'ledger_history_20261113/before_native_scope_01.json';assert not history.exists();shutil.copy2(ledger,history);l=read(ledger)
names=['prepare_native_scope_request.py','run_current_relaxed_queries_v2.py','run_native_scope_policy.py','run_native_scope_policy_v2.py','run_native_scope_policy_v3.py','report_native_scope_policy.py','diagnose_protected_critical_prefix.py','diagnose_protected_critical_prefix_v2.py','run_protected_joint_search.py','run_protected_native_control.py','report_protected_native_scope.py','export_native_scope_progress.py','native_scope_policy_summary_02.json','protected_native_scope_summary_01.json','native_timing_budget_scope_experiment_01.json','native_scope_request_validation_01/validation.json','current_sta_policy_native_continue_01/completion.json','current_sta_policy_native_R1_01/completion.json','current_sta_policy_native_target_only_01/failure.json','current_sta_policy_native_target_only_02/completion.json','protected_critical_prefix_dev_01/completion.json','protected_critical_prefix_dev_02/completion.json','protected_joint_scope_search_01/completion.json','protected_joint_scope_search_02/completion.json','protected_native_scope_dev_01/completion.json','paper/data/native_scope_policy_v14.csv','paper/data/native_scope_policy_discussion_v14.tex']
l['sources_sha256'].update({n:sha(D/n) for n in names});l['updated_at']=time.time();l['native_scope_policy']=dict(claims=['C93','C94','C95','C96'],summary='native_scope_policy_summary_02.json',conditional_reference='protected_native_scope_summary_01.json',next='native_timing_budget_scope_experiment_01.json',quality_promoted=False,new_work_pushed=False);write(ledger,l)
